  "published": "2026-07-01",
  "insights": [
   "The proprietary TYCCLES machine learning model for US Treasuries has transitioned from a 'max sell-off' regime to a 'moderate sell-off' regime as of 15 June 2026.",
   "A 'moderate sell-off' regime historically sees yields drift higher by 5-10bps across the curve, with 10Y yields rising ~15bp one month into the regime.",
   "The transition is driven by front-end/belly yield stabilization, decreased realized volatility at 10Y/30Y points, and curve flattening (12m5s and 10s30s).",
   "The regime is considered 'sticky' and typically lasts about two months before probabilities of transitioning to other regimes equalize.",
   "HSBC's rates strategists maintain a view of upward pressure on front-end yields, and the Multi-Asset team maintains a slight underweight stance on US Treasuries."
